    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.enumerate_all_cliques - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.enumerate_all_cliques.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.enumerate_all_cliques()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: List every clique of an undirected graph, smallest first.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.enumerate_all_cliques()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: List every clique of an undirected graph, smallest first.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.enumerate_all_cliques()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: List every clique of an undirected graph, smallest first.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nList every clique of an undirected graph, smallest first.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L34856-L34958){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.enumerate_all_cliques()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Enumerate all cliques](../assets/graphs/enumerate-all-cliques.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Left: a triangle of nodes 1, 2, 3. Right: its seven cliques as miniature triangles in rows by size, each clique in the accent color: the three single nodes [1], [2], [3], the three edges [1, 2], [1, 3], [2, 3], and the whole triangle [1, 2, 3].\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nUnlike `find_cliques()`, which reports only maximal cliques, this lists all of them:\nevery single node, every edge, every triangle, and so on, ordered by size. Counting\ncliques of each size gives the clique profile used in network comparison, motif-style\nstatistics and topological data analysis (the cliques are the simplices of the clique\ncomplex).\n\nThe number of cliques can be exponential in the size of the largest one, so use it on\nsparse or small graphs. Parallel edges count once and self-loops are ignored.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [list[list[int]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The cliques as lists of node IDs, in non-decreasing order of size.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is directed.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nA breadth-first expansion: each clique is extended only by common neighbors with a\nlarger ID than its last node, so every clique is produced exactly once, in the same\norder as NetworkX's `enumerate_all_cliques`.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~find_cliques`) \n\n:   List only the maximal cliques.\n\n[](`~list_triangles`) \n\n:   List the cliques of three.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA triangle `A`, `B`, `C` with a tail `C`-`D` has nine cliques: the four nodes, the four\nedges and the triangle, in order of size:\n\n::: {#30afe36d .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"A\"), (\"C\", \"D\")]\n)\n\nlabel = graph.get_label_from_id\n[[label(n) for n in c] for c in graph.enumerate_all_cliques()]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n[['A'],\n ['B'],\n ['C'],\n ['D'],\n ['A', 'B'],\n ['A', 'C'],\n ['B', 'C'],\n ['C', 'D'],\n ['A', 'B', 'C']]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Cliques inside cliques\n\nEvery subset of a clique is a clique, so a large one holds a great many. `les_miserables()`\nlinks two characters of Victor Hugo's novel when they appear in the same chapter. It has\n59 maximal cliques, but 2,922 cliques in all:\n\n::: {#6567c0f0 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfrom collections import Counter\n\nnovel = ec.les_miserables()\ncliques = novel.enumerate_all_cliques()\n\nlen(novel.find_cliques()), len(cliques)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(59, 2922)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nCounting them by size gives the network's clique profile. Most have four to six\ncharacters:\n\n::: {#d6a00215 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nCounter(len(clique) for clique in cliques)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\nCounter({5: 644,\n         4: 639,\n         6: 476,\n         3: 467,\n         2: 254,\n         7: 252,\n         8: 91,\n         1: 77,\n         9: 20,\n         10: 2})\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe two cliques of ten hold 1,023 cliques each. Both are at the barricade, and they share\neight characters: Gavroche and seven of the students of the Friends of the ABC. One adds\nMarius and Mabeuf, the other the students Prouvaire and Grantaire. Drawing the twelve of\nthem on their own:\n\n::: {#6f69751b .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfirst, second = [set(c) for c in cliques if len(c) == 10]\nlabel = novel.get_label_from_id\n\nbarricade = novel.subgraph(sorted(first | second))\nbarricade.set_node_attrs(\n    \"cliques\",\n    {label(n): \"both\" if n in first & second else \"one\"\n     for n in first | second},\n)\nbarricade.plot(color_by=\"cliques\", label_by=\"label\", seed=1)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"36.4 6.3 710.3 507.4\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"36.4\" y=\"6.3\" width=\"710.3\" height=\"507.4\" fill=\"var(--ect-3239c383)\"/>\n<line 